// expect: 7
// A refinement on one operand says nothing about its sibling: `n: Positive`
// proves the division total, and `t` may be anything — 0 here. The
// arithmetic unification used to carry `n`'s refinement onto `t`'s class,
// so `ratio` published `(t: Positive, n: Positive)` and `ratio(0, 5)` was
// REFUSED (E_RefinementRejected on the 0) — a correct program rejected
// because a sibling was over-demanded (P0, boot 13e8484a).
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn ratio(t, n: Positive) with !Trap = t / n

fn main() = ratio(0, 5) + 7
